================================================================================
ThemeForge Color Palettes / Theme Variants - Attribution
================================================================================

RouteWard integrates the 16 canonical ThemeForge palettes plus High Contrast:
- Dracula: canonical MIT palette by Zeno Rocha (https://github.com/dracula/dracula-theme).
- Drakul: WCAG AA-compliant Apache 2.0 sibling derived from Dracula by Julien Bombled
  (Comment lifted from #6272A4 to #B3BBD6).
- Striga, Cinder, Bracken, Tarn, Mortis, Slate, Voivode, Carmilla, Whitby, Vesper,
  Parchment, Folio, Wormwood, and Sconce: original Apache 2.0 palettes engineered
  from uniform Oklab targets by Julien Bombled.

================================================================================
WinDivert (Windows Packet Divert) - Dynamic Runtime Dependency (Windows)
================================================================================

On Windows, RouteWard supports transparent packet interception by dynamically
loading WinDivert.dll at runtime (via LoadLibraryW / GetProcAddress).
WinDivert is developed by Basil (https://github.com/basil00/WinDivert) and is
dual-licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (LGPLv3) or the
GNU General Public License v2 (GPLv2).

RouteWard uses WinDivert under the LGPLv3 dynamic linking terms:
- No WinDivert source code or binary artifacts are statically linked into
  RouteWard or committed to the repository.
- Users may obtain the official WinDivert 2.2.2-A binaries via
  tools/fetch-windivert.ps1 (with SHA-256 verification) or replace WinDivert.dll
  on disk with any compatible version.
- See third_party/windivert/LICENSE.md for the license text and source link.
